  <main_text>
    <l n="1">cuius rei etiã illa Ciceronis,</l>
    <l n="2">quę ex lib. de Off.II. subijciã,</l>
    <l n="3">documento sunt: Quæ autē</l>
    <l n="4">opera,inquit,non largitione,</l>
    <l n="5">beneficia dantur,hæc tum in</l>
    <l n="6">uniuersam Rempublicã, tũ</l>
    <l n="7">in singulos ciues conferūtur.</l>
    <l n="8">nam in Iure cauere, consilio</l>
    <l n="9">iuuare, atque hoc scientię</l>
    <l n="10">genere prodesse quãplurimis,</l>
    <l n="11">uehementer &amp; ad opes aug-</l>
    <l n="12">ēdas pertinet, &amp; ad gratiā.</l>
    <l n="13">Itaque cùm multa præclara</l>
    <l n="14">maiorũ, tum quàm optimè</l>
    <l n="15">constituti Iuris ciuilis sum-</l>
    <l n="16">mo semper in honore fuit co-</l>
    <l n="17">gnitio atque interpretatio:</l>
    <l n="18">quam quidē ante hanc con-</l>
    <l n="19">fusionem temporum in pos-</l>
